   "widgets_values": [
    "# cgi-042 · Binc stereo — fresh graph v01\n\n**One spine, nothing historical.** `LoadVideo` reads the APPROVED v03 take from `ComfyUI-Shared/input/shots/cgi-042/05-outputs/Approved/`. Everything to the right branches from `GetVideoComponents.images`.\n\n**Source (measured):** `cgi-042-pullback-4k-v03.mp4` — 3840x2160 HEVC `yuv420p10le`, range **tv**, matrix **bt709 (tagged)**,\n24/1, 241 f, AAC audio track present (ignore). Tagged → Comfy's decode to float32 is trustworthy; no colour declaration needed on this file.\n\n**Flow:** PASSTHROUGH (proof copy) · TRIM (window) → DEPTH (Binc DA2, local, sequence-normalised) → TEMPORAL (median-5 + no-lag EMA)\n→ STEREO (Binc: hull → DIBR → push-pull paint-in) → SBS + eye L + eye R videos, evidence PNGs, two text readouts.\n\n**Before first Queue**\n1. DEPTH node: `hf_repo_id` is pre-filled (`depth-anything/Depth-Anything-V2-Large-hf`) — transformers downloads ~1.3 GB into the HF cache on first run.\n   Prefer offline? put the HF folder in `models/depth_anything/` and pick it in `model`, clear `hf_repo_id`.\n2. TRIM is `108 / 25` (frames 109-133, centre f121). Set `0 / 241` for the full take **after** a 25-frame run looks right (241 × 4K float ≈ 24 GB per copy).\n3. `fps` is wired from the source into all three CreateVideo nodes — no hand-typed frame rate.\n\n**Read after Queue, in this order**\n1. `JITTER` — filtered mean should land ≤ ~0.9 levels (Kyle's v03 figure); raw will be ~4.\n2. `PARALLAX REPORT` — `summary.ok` must be true; `worst_pct` is what you compare to disparity measured on the v03 L/R masters.\n3. `parallax_vis` — near objects must be **DARK**. If bright → set `depth_polarity = near_is_dark` on STEREO.\n4. anaglyph at f121 (and move TRIM to 60/20 to see the f65–76 edge cluster + f72→73 step).\n\n**Status:** BUILT - NOT RUN. Package `ComfyUI-BincStereo` v0.2.0 headless-tested; first execution inside this build is this graph.\nFilmout path (SaveVideo codec auto) UNVERIFIED — outputs are review material."
   ],
   "title": "READ FIRST — cgi-042 · Binc stereo · fresh graph v01 (2026-10-10)"
